@*
    Organization View  (2026-11-02)

    Route: /OrganizationManagement/organization-view?code=<encrypted>

    PURPOSE
    -------
    A read-only, single page showing everything recorded for ONE
    organization. It is what a row click on Organization Management's
    landing list opens. Organization Setup stays what it has always been
    -- the edit / onboarding form -- and this page's Actions > Edit is how
    you get there. (The first cut of this change made Organization Setup
    itself render read-only; sir asked for a proper separate view page
    instead, which is this.)

    NO ID IN THE URL. The organization arrives inside the encrypted
    navigation code (?code=), the NavigationContextProtector envelope every
    other cross-screen drill in this app uses. Opened without one, the page
    says so rather than falling back to some organization.

    DATA SOURCES -- three reads, every one of them already existed. No new
    endpoint, no new stored procedure, no new column:
      * the organization row   -> POST {gateway}/organizations/query  { id }
                                  (migration 510's sp_org_organization_list,
                                  the same read the landing list uses -- it
                                  is where SpocName comes from)
      * attributes + subscribed
        releases               -> POST {gateway}/organization-setup/query
                                  (404's 'organization-setup' branch:
                                  table 2 = the metadata definitions with
                                  this organization's values, table 3 = the
                                  authority/artifact/release tree carrying
                                  IsSubscribed)
      * lookup labels          -> GET  {gateway}/lookups
                                  (Time Zone is stored as an id)

    The Actions button is the shared one -- wwwroot/js/Shared/page-actions-
    menu.js, window.gracPageActions.attach -- the same button and menu
    Practice / Gap / Task / Exception View carry. Nothing about it is
    re-implemented here.

    Styling follows gap-view.cshtml's read-only page: section headings over
    .ov-facts definition lists. Same visual language, no new design.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen
@{
    var permissions = ViewBag.Permissions as string[] ?? [];
    // The module root is the organization list (PracticeController.Index ->
    // ShowArea("organizations")). "/" when the module is served with no base
    // path. Built from AppBasePath rather than a tag helper for the reason
    // Manage.cshtml's Add Organization button documents: /OrganizationManagement
    // is a PathBase in a hosted deployment but a conventional route on a plain
    // host, and a tag helper can resolve against the Practice route instead.
    string appBasePathForLinks = Convert.ToString(ViewBag.AppBasePath) ?? string.Empty;
    var organizationListUrl = appBasePathForLinks.TrimEnd('/');
    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(organizationListUrl)) organizationListUrl = "/";
}

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1 id="ovHeading">Legal Entity</h1>
        <p id="ovSubHeading">Everything recorded for this organization, read-only.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex; gap:8px;">
        <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="ovActionsBtn" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-bolt" aria-hidden="true"></i> Actions
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:10px; margin-left:2px;"></i>
        </button>
        <a class="pm-button" href="@organizationListUrl">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> Back to Organizations
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="pm-panel" id="ovUnavailable" hidden>
    <div class="pm-empty">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-info pm-empty-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <h2 id="ovUnavailableTitle">Legal Entity not found.</h2>
        <p id="ovUnavailableBody">Open this page from the Organizations list.</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="pm-panel" id="ovRoot" hidden>

    <div class="pm-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between">
        <div>
            <span class="pm-badge" id="ovStatusChip">-</span>
            <strong id="ovTitle" style="margin-left:8px"></strong>
        </div>
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="ovRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
    </div>

    <h3 class="ov-section">Legal Entity Details</h3>
    <dl class="ov-facts" id="ovDetails"></dl>

    <h3 class="ov-section">Subscription</h3>
    <dl class="ov-facts" id="ovSubscription"></dl>

    <h3 class="ov-section">Address &amp; Locale</h3>
    <dl class="ov-facts ov-facts-wide" id="ovAddress"></dl>

    @* The metadata definitions and this organization's values, rendered
       straight from the API rows (MetadataName + DataType) rather than from
       a copy of practice.js's setupAttributeSchema -- one less place for the
       two to drift. Hidden when the organization has no attributes. *@
    <div id="ovAttributesWrap" hidden>
        <h3 class="ov-section">Organization Attributes</h3>
        <dl class="ov-facts" id="ovAttributes"></dl>
    </div>

    @* Subscribed releases, grouped Authority > Artifact, from the same tree
       Organization Setup's subscription panel reads (IsSubscribed). A list,
       not the landing list's "+N more" summary -- there is room here.
       Each release shows its release owner (2026-11-03), read from the
       subscribed-frameworks summary Standards & Frameworks uses. *@
    <h3 class="ov-section">Standards &amp; Frameworks</h3>
    <p class="pm-hint" id="ovFrameworksEmpty" hidden>This organization has no active repository subscriptions.</p>
    <div class="ov-frameworks" id="ovFrameworks"></div>

</section>

<style>
    /* Read-only facts panels, the same shape gap-view.cshtml uses for the
       same job -- section heading over a definition list on a tinted panel. */
    #ovRoot .ov-section {
        margin: 18px 0 8px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
        text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--fg-secondary);
    }
    #ovRoot .ov-facts {
        display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 260px));
        gap: 8px 20px; margin: 0 0 4px;
        padding: 12px 14px; background: var(--neutral-50); border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    }
    #ovRoot .ov-facts dt {
        font-size: 10px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--fg-muted);
    }
    #ovRoot .ov-facts dd {
        margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--neutral-700); overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        white-space: pre-wrap;
    }
    #ovRoot .ov-facts dd.ov-empty { color: var(--fg-subtle); font-style: italic; }
    #ovRoot .ov-facts.ov-facts-wide { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr)); }

    /* Authority > Artifact > releases. Indentation carries the hierarchy;
       the release versions are chips so one artifact with six releases
       stays one line deep. */
    #ovRoot .ov-frameworks {
        padding: 12px 14px; background: var(--neutral-50); border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    }
    #ovRoot .ov-authority { margin: 0 0 12px; }
    #ovRoot .ov-authority:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    #ovRoot .ov-authority-name {
        font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--neutral-700);
        text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em;
    }
    #ovRoot .ov-artifact { margin: 6px 0 0 14px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 10px; align-items: baseline; }
    #ovRoot .ov-artifact-name { font-size: 13px; color: var(--neutral-700); font-weight: 600; }
    #ovRoot .ov-release {
        display: inline-block; padding: 1px 9px; border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
        font-size: 11px; font-weight: 650;
        background: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); color: var(--fg-secondary);
    }
    /* Release owner beside each release chip (2026-11-03). */
    #ovRoot .ov-release-item { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 6px; }
    #ovRoot .ov-release-owner { font-size: 12px; color: var(--fg-secondary); }
    #ovRoot .ov-release-owner.ov-empty { color: var(--fg-subtle); font-style: italic; }
</style>

<script>
    // What the page needs from the server. The generic Manage layout's own
    // script block is not emitted for a workflow-screen partial (Manage.cshtml
    // returns before its @@section Scripts), so each partial exposes its own.
    window.pmApi = "@ViewBag.ApiBaseUrl";
    window.pmPermissions = @Html.Raw(System.Text.Json.JsonSerializer.Serialize(permissions));
</script>
<script src="~/js/Shared/page-actions-menu.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script src="~/js/Organization/organization-view.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
